  "summary_of_theorems": {
    "T1_prefix_demodulated_binary_sign_law": "For any label k with v_2(k) = ell - 1 - r, the prefix-demodulated quadrature score D_r(k, A, z; s_{<r}) = z phi_A(k s_{<r} / 2^ell) has pointwise mean (-1)^(s_r) * (v / 2) and variance 1/2 - v^2 / 4. This is an identity, not sampled shift recovery.",
    "T2_equal_valuation_cnot_pairing_dichotomy": "Merging any two labels k_1, k_2 with v_2(k_1) = v_2(k_2) = h < ell - 1 advances v_2(k_out) >= h + 1 on BOTH CNOT branches, with exact valuation h + 1 on one branch and >= h + 2 on the complementary branch.",
    "T3_sieve_depth_visibility_thresholds": "FULL balanced depth-d trees with nonzero equal-valuation inputs have 2^d leaves and visibility (1-p_bad)^(2^d). General trees use actual leaves L; valuation may jump."
  },
